com/kasavintest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kasavintest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kasavintest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kasavintest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kasavintest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kasavintest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kasavintest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kasavintest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kasavintest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kasavintest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-08T21:49:39Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T21:49:39Z","body":"> [@kasavin](https://github.com/kasavin) I don't think that's the case - the official documentations of GitHub and VS Code I linked in OP both explain how to change the model for code completion. So it was available before, unless both websites are misleading?\n\nHi @trymzet - sorry if I am being unclear - I think there are two questions in this thread:\n\n1. Can you change the model for code completion?\n2. Which models are available for code completion? \n \nWe introduced the model selector for code completion when the GPT-4o Copilot model was in preview and before the 3.5 Turbo-based model was retired. That way, it was possible to switch between the two to use either one. Now that the 3.5 Turbo-based model is retired, only the 4o Copilot model is available for code completion.\n\nThe picker UI should be visible again - I just tested in VS Code stable:\n\n<img width=\"601\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e06b6681-7bfe-41d0-8618-12a8b934e05e\" />\n\nBut this particular picker for completion never had Claude as an option. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2787739915/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2836838657","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/7052#issuecomment-2836838657","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/7052","id":2836838657,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6pFrkB","user":{"login":"j3g","id":117951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/117951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/j3g","html_url":"https://github.com/j3g","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j3g/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j3g/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j3g/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j3g/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j3g/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j3g/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j3g/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j3g/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j3g/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T22:06:14Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T22:06:14Z","body":"I also came here because documentation is confusing and the selector only has one option. I also want to change the code completion to a claude model, because in my experience it has better results for my project (flutter + dart). I understand you are concerned with latency, so maybe those models aren't fast enough for code completion\n\nI completely understand this is different from ask/edit/agent models which have their own lists of models","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https:/