le a new issue. Thank you again!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2843825402/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2914600186","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/7052#issuecomment-2914600186","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/7052","id":2914600186,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6tuUT6","user":{"login":"charles4221","id":15863771,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODYzNzcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15863771?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charles4221","html_url":"https://github.com/charles4221","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charles4221/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charles4221/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charles4221/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charles4221/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charles4221/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charles4221/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charles4221/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charles4221/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charles4221/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T01:22:59Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T01:23:07Z","body":"> The list of available models might vary based on your Copilot subscription and model availability\n\nBut this isn't true? I'm in an enterprise org with paid subscriptions and all models enabled, yet we still can only choose one option for the code completions model.\n\nI am confused as to why you even have documentation explaining how to switch the code completions model at all if we only have one option? I spent all morning trying to figure out why I can't switch the code completion model to Claude until I finally found this thread...\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2914600186/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/3031174644","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/7052#issuecomment-3031174644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/7052","id":3031174644,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc60rA30","user":{"login":"SiliconKidVP","id":199910709,"node_id":"U_kgDOC-plNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199910709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SiliconKidVP","html_url":"https://github.com/SiliconKidVP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SiliconKidVP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SiliconKidVP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SiliconKidVP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SiliconKidVP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SiliconKidVP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SiliconKidVP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SiliconKidVP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SiliconKidVP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SiliconKidVP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-03T07:24:30Z","updated_at":"2025-07-03T07:25:22Z","body":"This whole situation is very strange.\n\nI have been relying on Copilot code completion for months now and have always been under the distinct impression that the model I chose in the Copilot Chat window, at the bottom, was ALSO the model being used for everything else related to VS, including code completions.\n\nAnd the reason I was under that impression was because everything implies that. \n\nIf you click the GitHub Copilot button top right of Visual Studio and then click Settings, there is then an option to tick Enable Copilot Completions.\n\nThe direct implication of that menu structure and where it is positioned is that whatever model you have selected in the Copilot Chat window (which is the ONLY place I was aware you could even select an AI model until now) is the model that will be used for code completions.\n\nI didn't even realize there was a separate setting with a separate dropdown menu hiding under Options->GitHub->Copilot until now, and in fact that dropdown doesn't even have anything selected at the moment in my case.\n\nI cannot believe that this entire time GPT-4o has been handling code completions and I've basically paid for a Github Copilot Pro license for nothing, because I almost never chat with the AI, my primary use for it is to sit and watch me and make code suggestions, and handle code completion, without me asking it anything.\n\nI was also under the impression that any interaction I did explicitly have with the model I had selected in the Copilot Chat window was contributing to that model's domain knowledge and helping it to be more effective when it makes suggestions and handles code completion.\n\nClearly not, since a completely different model is doing the code completions, which means there is no shared context, unless I'm missing something.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/3031174644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]}